## Utility scripts

### free_libvirt_raw_disk.py

Inspects and frees Coriolis libvirt raw disk allocations that are stuck in
`attached` or `claimed` state. This can happen when a deployment is created
without cloning disks: the replicated volumes are attached directly to the
migrated VM, and after the VM is deleted they remain reserved in the SQLite DB,
preventing new transfers from picking them up.

    # List all raw disks and their current status
    python3 /root/free_libvirt_raw_disk.py list

    # List only stuck disks
    python3 /root/free_libvirt_raw_disk.py list --status attached
    python3 /root/free_libvirt_raw_disk.py list --status claimed

    # Free a specific disk by WWN
    python3 /root/free_libvirt_raw_disk.py free --wwn <wwn>

    # Free all stuck disks (shows a confirmation prompt)
    python3 /root/free_libvirt_raw_disk.py free --all
